{"from": "artifact:theodotos-inscription", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-12-38-39-scribes-honor-garments", "grade": "C", "note": "A first-century Jerusalem inscription for a synagogue built for reading and teaching attests the synagogue institution whose best seats are at issue; it says nothing about seating rank or robes - the same C the Matthew 23 runner gave on the shared best-seats claim."}
{"from": "artifact:tyrian-shekel", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-12-41-treasury-chests", "grade": "C", "note": "Tyrian shekels were specifically required for the Temple tax; the thirteen chests received the collected shekels - the depositing of coin Mark 12:41 describes. It attests the coin economy, not the treasury furniture or the widow's lepta."}
